  {
    "code": "MACRO-16",
    "status": "EXPERIMENTAL_CANDIDATE",
    "output": "tmp\\pdf_accessibility\\owner_qa_remediation_v1\\batches\\batch1_high\\revisions\\fc6bdef0fdc4cb5fa2e6b1e819126f8bf94aef4df1b32c6cf93394deed2cc46f\\after\\MACRO-16.pdf",
    "tagCount": 35,
    "mcids": 31,
    "unassignedMeaningfulBlocks": 0,
    "inlineFormulaSemantics": "SOURCE_BOUND_RUNS",
    "transcript": [
      {
        "role": "H1",
        "text": "Labor-Market Institutions",
        "node": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "P",
        "text": "MACROECONOMICS",
        "node": 1
      },
      {
        "role": "P",
        "text": "MACRO-16",
        "node": 2
      },
      {
        "role": "P",
        "text": "Time: 5 minutes",
        "node": 3
      },
      {
        "role": "P",
        "text": "Outcome: Analyze minimum wages, unions, job search, and efficiency wages.",
        "node": 4
      },
      {
        "role": "P",
        "text": "Difficulty: Intermediate",
        "node": 5
      },
      {
        "role": "H2",
        "text": "THE CORE IDEA",
        "node": 6
      },
      {
        "role": "P",
        "text": "Labor-market institutions change wages, hiring, search incentives, and the balance between labor supplied and labor demanded. Efficiency wages can improve effort and reduce turnover. A binding minimum wage can create a surplus of labor, meaning more workers want jobs than firms want to hire. Unemployment insurance can support job seekers, but may also reduce urgency to accept a job quickly.",
        "node": 7
      },
      {
        "role": "H2",
        "text": "HOW TO RECOGNIZE IT",
        "node": 8
      },
      {
        "role": "Lbl",
        "text": "•",
        "node": 11
      },
      {
        "role": "LBody",
        "text": "A binding minimum wage can create a surplus of labor, meaning more workers want jobs than firms want to hire.",
        "node": 12
      },
      {
        "role": "Lbl",
        "text": "•",
        "node": 14
      },
      {
        "role": "LBody",
        "text": "Unemployment insurance can support job seekers, but may also reduce urgency to accept a job quickly.",
        "node": 15
      },
      {
        "role": "Lbl",
        "text": "•",
        "node": 17
      },
      {
        "role": "LBody",
        "text": "A firm raises wages above equilibrium and worker effort rises enough to improve productivity, but fewer workers are hired at the higher wage.",
        "node": 18
      },
      {
        "role": "Lbl",
        "text": "•",
        "node": 20
      },
      {
        "role": "LBody",
        "text": "Unemployment insurance can reduce the cost of continued job search, which may lengthen unemployment spells.",
        "node": 21
      },
      {
        "role": "Lbl",
        "text": "•",
        "node": 23
      },
      {
        "role": "LBody",
        "text": "Union wage bargaining can raise wages above equilibrium and reduce the quantity of labor demanded.",
        "node": 24
      },
      {
        "role": "H2",
        "text": "WATCH OUT",
        "node": 25
      },
      {
        "role": "P",
        "text": "Do not forget that a binding wage floor creates a surplus when labor supplied exceeds labor demanded. A binding minimum wage can create a surplus of labor, meaning more workers want jobs than firms want to hire.",
        "node": 26
      },
      {
        "role": "H2",
        "text": "WORKED EXAMPLE: BINDING MINIMUM WAGE",
        "node": 27
      },
      {
        "role": "Figure",
        "text": "Wage per hour vertical, quantity of labor in workers horizontal. Labor supply slopes up and demand down, meeting at wage 12 and 105 workers. A binding minimum wage of 15 is above equilibrium. At that wage QD is 90 and QS is 120; a bracket marks a labor surplus of 30 workers.",
        "node": 28
      },
      {
        "role": "P",
        "text": "At a binding minimum wage, 120 workers want jobs and firms hire 90. The labor surplus is 120 - 90 = 30 workers. The wage is held above equilibrium, so the quantity of labor supplied exceeds the quantity demanded.",
        "node": 29
      },
      {
        "role": "H2",
        "text": "CHECK YOURSELF",
        "node": 30
      },
      {
        "role": "P",
        "text": "Why can more generous unemployment insurance lengthen some unemployment spells even while protecting workers?",
        "node": 31
      },
      {
        "role": "H2",
        "text": "READY?",
        "node": 32
      },
      {
        "role": "P",
        "text": "Return to the game and master this concept.",
        "node": 33
      }
    ],
